40.def:
from hagos (an awful thing) (compare 53, 2282); sacred (physically,
pure, morally blameless or religious, ceremonially,
consecrated):--(most) holy (one, thing), saint.

96.def:
from 1 (as a negative particle) and 1384; unapproved, i.e. rejected;
by implication, worthless (literally or morally):--castaway, rejected,
reprobate.

104.def:
from an obsolete primary noun (apparently meaning continued duration);
"ever,"by qualification regularly; by implication, earnestly;
--always, ever.

111.def:
from 1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of themis (statute;
from the base of 5087); illegal; by implication,
flagitious:--abominable, unlawful thing.

138.def:
probably akin to 142; to take for oneself, i.e. to prefer:--choose.
Some of the forms are borrowed from a cognate hellomai hel'-lom-ahee;
which is otherwise obsolete.

160.def:
from a compound of 1 (as a negative particle) and 5316 (compare 1810)
(meaning non-apparent); unexpected, i.e. (adverbially)
suddenly:--sudden, unawares.

211.def:
neuter of alabastros (of uncertain derivation), the name of a stone;
properly, an "alabaster" box, i.e. (by extension) a perfume vase (of
any material):--(alabaster) box.

276.def:
from 1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of 3346;
unchangeable, or (neuter as abstract)
unchangeability:--immutable(-ility).

318.def:
from 303 and the base of 43; constraint (literally or figuratively);
by implication, distress:--distress, must needs, (of)
necessity(-sary), needeth, needful.

350.def:
from 303 and 2919; properly, to scrutinize, i.e. (by implication)
investigate, interrogate, determine:--ask, question, discern, examine,
judge, search.

378.def:
from 303 and 4137; to complete; by implication, to occupy, supply;
figuratively, to accomplish (by coincidence ot obedience):--fill up,
fulfill, occupy, supply.

384.def:
from 303 (in the sense of reversal) and a derivative of 4632;
properly, to pack up (baggage), i.e. (by implication, and
figuratively) to upset:--subvert.

472.def:
from 473 and the middle voice of 2192; to hold oneself opposite to,
i.e. (by implication) adhere to; by extension to care for:--hold fast,
hold to, support.

505.def:
from 1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of 5271;
undissembled, i.e. sincere:--without dissimulation (hypocrisy),
unfeigned.

506.def:
from 1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of 5293;
unsubdued, i.e. insubordinate (in fact or temper):--disobedient, that
is not put under, unruly.

568.def:
from 575 and 2192; (actively) to have out, i.e. receive in full;
(intransitively) to keep (oneself) away, i.e. be distant (literally or
figuratively):--be, have, receive.

652.def:
from 649; a delegate; specially, an ambassador of the Gospel;
officially a commissioner of Christ ("apostle") (with miraculous
powers):--apostle, messenger, he that is sent.

677.def:
from 1 (as a negative particle) and a presumed derivative of 4350;
actively, inoffensive, i.e. not leading into sin; passively,
faultless, i.e. not led into sin:--none (void of, without) offence.

749.def:
from 746 and 2409; the high-priest (literally, of the Jews, typically,
Christ); by extension a chief priest:--chief (high) priest, chief of
the priests.

761.def:
from 1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of 4531; unshaken,
i.e. (by implication) immovable (figuratively):--which cannot be
moved, unmovable.

786.def:
from 1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of 4689; literally,
without libation (which usually accompanied a treaty), i.e. (by
implication) truceless:--implacable, truce-breaker.

795.def:
from a compound of 1 (as a negative particle) and stoichos (an aim);
to miss the mark, i.e. (figuratively) deviate from truth:--err,
swerve.

816.def:
from a compound of 1 (as a particle of union) and teino (to stretch);
to gaze intently:--behold earnestly (stedfastly), fasten (eyes), look
(earnestly, stedfastly, up stedfastly), set eyes.

847.def:
genitive (i.e. possessive) of 846, used as an adverb of location;
properly, belonging to the same spot, i.e. in this (or that)
place:--(t-)here.

868.def:
from 575 and 2476; to remove, i.e. (actively) instigate to revolt;
usually (reflexively) to desist, desert, etc.:--depart, draw (fall)
away, refrain, withdraw self.

922.def:
probably from the same as 939 (through the notion of going down;
compare 899); weight; in the New Testament only, figuratively, a load,
abundance, authority:--burden(-some), weight.

1035.def:
from the base of 977; (abstractly) eating (literally or figuratively);
by extension (concretely) food (literally or figuratively):--eating,
food, meat.

1067.def:
of Hebrew origin (1516 and 2011); valley of (the son of) Hinnom;
ge-henna (or Ge-Hinnom), a valley of Jerusalem, used (figuratively) as
a name for the place (or state) of everlasting punishment:--hell.

1085.def:
from 1096; "kin" (abstract or concrete, literal or figurative,
individual or collective):--born, country(-man), diversity,
generation, kind(-red), nation, offspring, stock.

1106.def:
from 1097; cognition, i.e. (subjectively) opinion, or (objectively)
resolve (counsel, consent, etc.):--advice, + agree, judgment, mind,
purpose, will.

1247.def:
from 1249; to be an attendant, i.e. wait upon (menially or as a host,
friend, or (figuratively) teacher); technically, to act as a Christian
deacon:--(ad-)minister (unto), serve, use the office of a deacon.

1261.def:
from 1260; discussion, i.e. (internal) consideration (by implication,
purpose), or (external) debate:--dispute, doubtful(-ing), imagination,
reasoning, thought.

1290.def:
from 1289; dispersion, i.e. (specially and concretely) the (converted)
Israelite resident in Gentile countries:--(which are) scattered
(abroad).

1330.def:
from 1223 and 2064; to traverse (literally):--come, depart, go (about,
abroad, everywhere, over, through, throughout), pass (by, over,
through, throughout), pierce through, travel, walk through.

1336.def:
neuter of a compound of 1223 and a derivative of an alternate of 5342;
carried through, i.e. (adverbially with 1519 and 3588 prefixed)
perpetually:--+ continually, for ever.

1388.def:
from an obsolete primary verb, dello (probably meaning to decoy;
compare 1185); a trick (bait), i.e. (figuratively) wile:--craft,
deceit, guile, subtilty.

1401.def:
from 1210; a slave (literal or figurative, involuntary or voluntary;
frequently, therefore in a qualified sense of subjection or
subserviency):--bond(-man), servant.

1484.def:
probably from 1486; a race (as of the same habit), i.e. a tribe;
specially, a foreign (non-Jewish) one (usually, by implication,
pagan):--Gentile, heathen, nation, people.

1544.def:
from 1537 and 906; to eject (literally or figuratively):--bring forth,
cast (forth, out), drive (out), expel, leave, pluck (pull, take,
thrust) out, put forth (out), send away (forth, out).

1567.def:
from 1537 and 2212; to search out, i.e. (figuratively)investigate,
crave, demand, (by Hebraism) worship:--en- (re-)quire, seek after
(carefully, diligently).

1622.def:
from 1537; the exterior; figuratively (as a preposition) aside from,
besides:--but, except(-ed), other than, out of, outside, unless,
without.

1689.def:
from 1722 and 991; to look on, i.e. (relatively) to observe fixedly,
or (absolutely) to discern clearly:--behold, gaze up, look upon,
(could) see.

1705.def:
or empletho em-play'-tho

from 1722 and the base of 4118;to fill in (up), i.e. (by implication)
to satisfy (literally or figuratively):--fill.

1735.def:
third person singular present of a compound of 1722 and 1209;
(impersonally) it is accepted in, i.e. admitted (possible):--can (+
not) be.

1793.def:
from 1722 and 5177; to chance upon, i.e. (by implication) confer with;
by extension to entreat (in favor or against):--deal with, make
intercession.

1885.def:
from a compound of 1909 and 757 (meaning a governor of a district,
"eparch"); a special region of government, i.e. a Roman
præfecture:--province.

1910.def:
from 1909 and the base of 939; to walk upon, i.e. mount, ascend,
embark, arrive:--come (into), enter into, go abroad, sit upon, take
ship.

1945.def:
from 1909 and 2749; to rest upon (literally or figuratively):--impose,
be instant, (be) laid (there-, up-)on, (when) lay (on), lie (on),
press upon.

1984.def:
from 1980; inspection (for relief); by implication, superintendence;
specially, the Christian "episcopate":--the office of a "bishop",
bishoprick, visitation.

2005.def:
from 1909 and 5055; to fulfill further (or completely), i.e. execute;
by implication, to terminate, undergo:--accomplish, do, finish, (make)
(perfect), perform(X -ance).

2078.def:
a superlative probably from 2192 (in the sense of contiguity);
farthest, final (of place or time):--ends of, last, latter end,
lowest, uttermost.

2106.def:
from 2095 and 1380; to think well of, i.e. approve (an act);
specially, to approbate (a person or thing):--think good, (be well)
please(-d), be the good (have, take) pleasure, be willing.

2107.def:
from a presumed compound of 2095 and the base of 1380; satisfaction,
i.e. (subjectively) delight, or (objectively) kindness, wish,
purpose:--desire, good pleasure (will), X seem good.

2127.def:
from a compound of 2095 and 3056; to speak well of, i.e. (religiously)
to bless (thank or invoke a benediction upon, prosper):--bless,
praise.

2159.def:
adverb from a compound of 2095 and a derivative of teino (to stretch);
in a well-strung manner, i.e. (figuratively) intensely (in a good
sense, cogently; in a bad one, fiercely):--mightily, vehemently.

2225.def:
from the same as 2226 and a derivative of 1096; to engender alive,
i.e. (by analogy) to rescue (passively, be saved) from death:--live,
preserve.

2270.def:
from the same as 2272; to keep still (intransitively), i.e. refrain
from labor, meddlesomeness or speech:--cease, hold peace, be quiet,
rest.

2469.def:
of Hebrew origin (probably 377 and 7149); inhabitant of Kerioth;
Iscariotes (i.e. Keriothite), an epithet of Judas the
traitor:--Iscariot.

2479.def:
from a derivative of is (force; compare eschon, a form of 2192);
forcefulness (literally or figuratively):--ability, might(-ily),
power, strength.

2525.def:
from 2596 and 2476; to place down (permanently), i.e. (figuratively)
to designate, constitute, convoy:--appoint, be, conduct, make, ordain,
set.

2549.def:
from 2556; badness, i.e. (subjectively) depravity, or (actively)
malignity, or (passively) trouble:--evil, malice(-iousness),
naughtiness, wickedness.

2727.def:
from 2596 and 2279; to sound down into the ears, i.e. (by implication)
to indoctrinate ("catechize") or (genitive case) to apprise
of:--inform, instruct, teach.

2744.def:
from some (obsolete) base akin to that of aucheo (to boast) and 2172;
to vaunt (in a good or a bad sense):--(make) boast, glory, joy,
rejoice.

2746.def:
from 2744; boasting (properly, the act; by implication, the object),
in a good or a bad sense:--boasting, whereof I may glory, glorying,
rejoicing.

2842.def:
from 2844; partnership, i.e. (literally) participation, or (social)
intercourse, or (pecuniary) benefaction:--(to) communicate(-ation),
communion, (contri-)distribution, fellowship.

2865.def:
from a primary komeo (to tend, i.e. take care of); properly, to
provide for, i.e. (by implication) to carry off (as if from harm;
genitive case obtain):--bring, receive.

2873.def:
from 2875; a cut, i.e. (by analogy) toil (as reducing the strength),
literally or figuratively; by implication, pains:--labour, + trouble,
weariness.

2889.def:
probably from the base of 2865; orderly arrangement, i.e. decoration;
by implication, the world (in a wide or narrow sense, including its
inhabitants, literally or figuratively (morally)):--adorning, world.

2962.def:
from kuros (supremacy); supreme in authority, i.e. (as noun)
controller; by implication, Master (as a respectful title):-- God,
Lord, master, Sir.

2986.def:
from the same as 2985; radiant; by analogy, limpid; figuratively,
magnificent or sumptuous (in appearance):--bright, clear, gay, goodly,
gorgeous, white.

3075.def:
middle voice from a probably derivative of 3089 (meaning filth);
properly, to soil, i.e. (figuratively) insult (maltreat):--make havock
of.

3114.def:
from the same as 3116; to be long-spirited, i.e. (objectively)
forbearing or (subjectively) patient:--bear (suffer) long, be
longsuffering, have (long) patience, be patient, patiently endure.

3342.def:
from 3326 and a form of 4862; betwixt (of place or person); (of time)
as adjective, intervening, or (by implication) adjoining:--between,
mean while, next.

3345.def:
from 3326 and a derivative of 4976; to transfigure or disguise;
figuratively, to apply (by accommodation):--transfer, transform
(self).

3350.def:
from a derivative of a compound of 3326 and 3624; a change of abode,
i.e. (specially), expatriation:--X brought, carried(-ying) away
(in-)to.

3403.def:
a prolonged form of 3415 (from which some of the tenses are borrowed);
to remind, i.e. (middle voice) to recall to mind:--be mindful,
remember.

3501.def:
including the comparative neoteros neh-o'-ter-os; a primary word;
"new", i.e. (of persons) youthful, or (of things) fresh; figuratively,
regenerate:--new, young.

3549.def:
from 3550; to legislate, i.e. (passively) to have (the Mosaic)
enactments injoined, be sanctioned (by them):--establish, receive the
law.

3586.def:
from another form of the base of 3582; timber (as fuel or material);
by implication, a stick, club or tree or other wooden article or
substance:--staff, stocks, tree, wood.

3614.def:
from 3624; properly, residence (abstractly), but usually (concretely)
an abode (literally or figuratively); by implication, a family
(especially domestics):--home, house(-hold).

3619.def:
feminine (abstract) of a compound of 3624 and the base of 1430;
architecture, i.e. (concretely) a structure; figuratively,
confirmation:--building, edify(-ication, -ing).

3697.def:
from 3739 and 4169; of what kind that, i.e. how (as) great (excellent)
(specially, as an indefinite correlative to the definite antecedent
5108 of quality):--what manner (sort) of, such as whatsoever.

3718.def:
from a compound of 3717 and the base of 5114, to make a straight cut,
i.e. (figuratively) to dissect (expound) correctly (the divine
message):--rightly divide.

3735.def:
probably from an obsolete oro (to rise or "rear"; perhaps akin to 142;
compare 3733); a mountain (as lifting itself above the plain): -hill,
mount(-ain).

3788.def:
from 3700; the eye (literally or figuratively); by implication,
vision; figuratively, envy (from the jealous side-glance):--eye,
sight.

3796.def:
from the same as 3694 (through the idea of backwardness);
(adverbially) late in the day; by extension, after the close of the
day:--(at) even, in the end.

3809.def:
from 3811; tutorage, i.e. education or training; by implication,
disciplinary correction:--chastening, chastisement, instruction,
nurture.

3813.def:
neuter diminutive of 3816; a childling (of either sex), i.e.
(properly), an infant, or (by extension) a half-grown boy or girl;
figuratively, an immature Christian:--(little, young) child, damsel.

3819.def:
probably another form for 3825 (through the idea of retrocession);
(adverbially) formerly, or (by relatively) sometime since;
(elliptically as adjective) ancient:--any while, a great while ago,
(of) old, in time past.

3829.def:
neuter of a presumed compound of 3956 and a derivative of 1209;
all-receptive, i.e. a public lodging-place (caravanserai or
khan):--inn.

3860.def:
from 3844 and 1325; to surrender, i.e yield up, intrust,
transmit:--betray, bring forth, cast, commit, deliver (up), give
(over, up), hazard, put in prison, recommend.

3870.def:
from 3844 and 2564; to call near, i.e. invite, invoke (by imploration,
hortation or consolation):--beseech, call for, (be of good) comfort,
desire, (give) exhort(-ation), intreat, pray.

3928.def:
from 3844 and 2064; to come near or aside, i.e. to approach (arrive),
go by (or away), (figuratively) perish or neglect, (causative)
avert:--come (forth), go, pass (away, by, over), past, transgress.

3930.def:
from 3844 and 2192; to hold near, i.e. present, afford, exhibit,
furnish occasion:--bring, do, give, keep, minister, offer, shew, +
trouble.

3952.def:
from the present participle of 3918; a being near, i.e. advent (often,
return; specially, of Christ to punish Jerusalem, or finally the
wicked); (by implication) physically, aspect:--coming, presence.

4014.def:
from 4012 and 138 (including its alternate); to remove all around,
i.e. unveil, cast off (anchor); figuratively, to expiate:--take away
(up).

4024.def:
from 4012 and 2224; to gird all around, i.e. (middle voice or passive)
to fasten on one's belt (literally or figuratively):--gird (about,
self).

4066.def:
from 4012 and 5561; around the region, i.e. circumjacent (as noun,
with 1093 implied vicinity):--country (round) about, region (that
lieth) round about.

4106.def:
feminine of 4108 (as abstractly); objectively, fraudulence;
subjectively, a straying from orthodoxy or piety:--deceit, to deceive,
delusion, error.

4141.def:
apparently another form of 4111 (through the idea of flattening out);
to pound, i.e. (figuratively) to inflict with (calamity):--smite.
Compare 5180.

4149.def:
from the base of 4130; wealth (as fulness), i.e. (literally) money,
possessions, or (figuratively) abundance, richness, (specially),
valuable bestowment:--riches.

4152.def:
from 4151; non-carnal, i.e. (humanly) ethereal (as opposed to gross),
or (daemoniacally) a spirit (concretely), or (divinely) supernatural,
regenerate, religious:--spiritual. Compare 5591.

4218.def:
from the base of 4225 and 5037; indefinite adverb, at some time,
ever:--afore-(any, some-)time(-s), at length (the last), (+ n- )ever,
in the old time, in time past, once, when.

4221.def:
neuter of a derivative of the alternate of 4095; a drinking-vessel; by
extension, the contents thereof, i.e. a cupful (draught);
figuratively, a lot or fate:--cup.

4270.def:
from 4253 and 1125; to write previously; figuratively, to announce,
prescribe:--before ordain, evidently set forth, write (afore,
aforetime).

4286.def:
from 4388; a setting forth, i.e. (figuratively) proposal (intention);
specially, the show-bread (in the Temple) as exposed before
God:--purpose, shew(-bread).

4327.def:
from 4314 and 1209; to admit (to intercourse, hospitality, credence,
or (figuratively) endurance); by implication, to await (with
confidence or patience):--accept, allow, look (wait) for, take.

4350.def:
from 4314 and 2875; to strike at, i.e. surge against (as water);
specially, to stub on, i.e. trip up (literally or figuratively):--beat
upon, dash, stumble (at).

4369.def:
from 4314 and 5087; to place additionally, i.e. lay beside, annex,
repeat:--add, again, give more, increase, lay unto, proceed further,
speak to any more.

4371.def:
neuter of a presumed derivative of a compound of 4314 and 5315;
something eaten in addition to bread, i.e. a relish (specially, fish;
compare 3795):--meat.

4531.def:
from 4535; to waver, i.e. agitate, rock, topple or (by implication)
destroy; figuratively, to disturb, incite:--move, shake (together),
which can(-not) be shaken, stir up.

4710.def:
from 4692; "speed", i.e. (by implication) despatch, eagerness,
earnestness:--business, (earnest) care(-fulness), diligence,
forwardness, haste.

4758.def:
from a compound of the base of 4756 and 3004 (in its original sense);
to gather (or select) as a warrior, i.e. enlist in the army:--choose
to be a soldier.

4815.def:
from 4862 and 2983; to clasp, i.e. seize (arrest, capture); specially,
to conceive (literally or figuratively); by implication, to
aid:--catch, conceive, help, take.

4864.def:
from (the reduplicated form of) 4863; an assemblage of persons;
specially, a Jewish "synagogue" (the meeting or the place); by
analogy, a Christian church:--assembly, congregation, synagogue.

4904.def:
from a presumed compound of 4862 and the base of 2041; a co-laborer,
i.e. coadjutor:--companion in labour, (fellow-)helper(-labourer,
-worker), labourer together with, workfellow.

4944.def:
from 4862 and 5605; to have (parturition) pangs in company (concert,
simultaneously) with, i.e. (figuratively) to sympathize (in
expectation of relief from suffering):--travail in pain together.

4980.def:
from 4981; to take a holiday, i.e. be at leisure for (by implication,
devote oneself wholly to); figuratively, to be vacant (of a
house):--empty, give self.

4982.def:
from a primary sos (contraction for obsolete saos, "safe"); to save,
i.e. deliver or protect (literally or figuratively):--heal, preserve,
save (self), do well, be (make) whole.

5012.def:
from a compound of 5011 and the base of 5424; humiliation of mind,
i.e. modesty:--humbleness of mind, humility (of mind, loneliness (of
mind).

5056.def:
from a primary tello (to set out for a definite point or goal);
properly, the point aimed at as a limit, i.e. (by implication) the
conclusion of an act or state (termination (literally, figuratively or
indefinitely), result (immediate, ultimate or prophetic), purpose);
specially, an impost or levy (as paid):--+ continual, custom,
end(-ing), finally, uttermost. Compare 5411.

5092.def:
from 5099; a value, i.e. money paid, or (concretely and collectively)
valuables; by analogy, esteem (especially of the highest degree), or
the dignity itself:--honour, precious, price, some.

5143.def:
apparently a primary verb (properly, threcho; compare 2359); which
uses dremo drem'-o (the base of 1408) as alternate in certain tenses;
to run or walk hastily (literally or figuratively):--have course, run.

5187.def:
from a derivative of 5188; to envelop with smoke, i.e. (figuratively)
to inflate with self-conceit:--high-minded, be lifted up with pride,
be proud.

5198.def:
from 5199; to have sound health, i.e. be well (in body); figuratively,
to be uncorrupt (true in doctrine):--be in health, (be safe and)
sound, (be) whole(-some).

5215.def:
apparently from a simpler (obsolete) form of hudeo (to celebrate;
probably akin to 103; compare 5667); a "hymn" or religious ode (one of
the Psalms):--hymn.

5235.def:
from 5228 and 906; to throw beyod the usual mark, i.e. (figuratively)
to surpass (only active participle supereminent):--exceeding, excel,
pass.

5274.def:
from 5259 and 2983; to take from below, i.e. carry upward;
figuratively, to take up, i.e. continue a discourse or topic;
mentally, to assume (presume):--answer, receive, suppose.

5278.def:
from 5259 and 3306; to stay under (behind), i.e. remain; figuratively,
to undergo, i.e. bear (trials), have fortitude, persevere:--abide,
endure, (take) patient(-ly), suffer, tarry behind.

5302.def:
from 5306; to be later, i.e. (by implication) to be inferior;
generally, to fall short (be deficient):--come behind (short), be
destitute, fail, lack, suffer need, (be in) want, be the worse.

5311.def:
from a derivative of 5228; elevation, i.e. (abstractly) altitude,
(specially), the sky, or (figuratively) dignity:--be exalted, height,
(on) high.

5406.def:
from 5408; a murderer (always of criminal (or at least intentional)
homicide; which 443 does not necessarily imply; while 4607 is a
special term for a public bandit):--murderer.

5421.def:
of uncertain derivation; a hole in the ground (dug for obtaining or
holding water or other purposes), i.e. a cistern or well;
figuratively, an abyss (as a prison):--well, pit.

5449.def:
from 5453; growth (by germination or expansion), i.e. (by implication)
natural production (lineal descent); by extension, a genus or sort;
figuratively, native disposition, constitution or usage:--(man-)kind,
nature(-al).

5467.def:
perhaps from 5465 through the idea of reducing the strength;
difficult, i.e. dangerous, or (by implication) furious:--fierce,
perilous.

5530.def:
middle voice of a primary verb (perhaps rather from 5495, to handle);
to furnish what is needed; (give an oracle, "graze" (touch slightly),
light upon, etc.), i.e. (by implication) to employ or (by extension)
to act towards one in a given manner:--entreat, use. Compare 5531;
